From 4f473b833872267223e5973cdb1a0bdc5d82a1c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 03:19:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] UI patch

Allow Rendering/UI to build with the Mac OS X 10.5/10.6 SDK and gcc.

Rebased onto 9.7.1, which added vtkCocoaHardwareView and
vtkCocoaHardwareWindow (used by the WebGPU backend). These get the same
treatment as vtkCocoaGLView: no CAMetalLayer, @available, @autoreleasepool,
collection literals or fast enumeration on old SDKs; NSDraggingDestination
is informal before 10.7; the window delegate gets an explicit ivar for
the fragile (32-bit) runtime; the 10.7+ backing-store APIs go through the
compatibility helpers.

The backing-store helpers no longer cast objc_msgSend by hand. That picked
the wrong variant for struct returns: on ppc every struct (including
NSPoint/NSSize) is returned in memory and needs objc_msgSend_stret, and on
i386/x86_64 NSRect does too. The methods are now declared in categories
for SDKs < 10.7 so the compiler emits the right send, and are only called
when the receiver responds to them.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
